verdicts.reason:
This fold is a withholding label, not an organization, so dropping it costs no real party.

1. **The entry.** batch-ne-06.json:1467 has exactly one spelling, "Withheld Section94 Supplier 2", classed placeholder. It has 1 org, 2 mentions and roles {Tenderer: 2}. The roles were the same 2 Tenderer rows in u3's plan-2265, when the org had 14 mentions. The org is in the identified list as 31548264 GB, GBPPONPGYY2165QXNQ, with 2 mentions.

2. **Why the predicate drops it.** In crates/ingest/src/partyname.rs, classify() takes these steps:
   - no void stem matches;
   - it is not a section-reference pointer;
   - placeholder_hit finds the anchored " withheld" stem (PLACEHOLDER_STEMS, StemAt::Start) opening the fold;
   - " withheld" is not in POINTER_STEMS, so the pointer_names keep rule (the AwardSummary keep) cannot fire;
   - it is a Start stem, so named_before does not apply;
   - summary_shape is false, which the computed class confirms.
   The class is Placeholder. The party has no other spelling, so every name is Placeholder and the fold drops it.

3. **The spelling names no one.** It is the Procurement Act 2023 s.94 withheld-supplier label. The "2" numbers the second withheld supplier, the same way as its sibling "Withheld Section94 Supplier" (PBXY-3232-WNHZ, org 30914328). That PPON was read on 2026-10-12 and stands for unrelated suppliers (partyname.rs:278 comment). A third registration of the same kind exists: "Withheld for Security Reasons - Section 94 Supplier" (GBPPONPMBM2912XLDW, org 31567546).

4. **The PPON keys no real-named org.** The 2026-09-30 census of GB national orgs (.scratch/tender-db/452-census/gb-orgs-2026-09-30.jsonl, 58,938 rows) has GBPPONPGYY2165QXNQ on one row only: org 31548264 "Withheld Section94 Supplier 2" (line 43538). No real supplier holds it. The u3 lists read (u3/reads-wf_a3c63d17.json) reached the same conclusion for both Section94 PPONs.

5. **Placeholders get no identifier guard, by decision.** unit1-decision.md §3 says Placeholder gets no identifier guard and names exactly this org ("Withheld Section94 Supplier 2 carries another (31548264, review read)"). The reasoning there is that an identifier beside a withheld name belongs to the placeholder, not to a supplier.

**What is still open.** The runbook's live organizations_identity lookup and the read of the 2 mention names are procedural checks that were not run here (no prod reads were allowed). The local evidence (the name itself, a single-holder PPON in the census, and the sibling PPON pattern) leaves no sign of a real supplier, and no keep test is warranted. Even if the PPON were later found on a real-named org, the published name in these 2 Tenderer slots withholds the supplier, so the slot still names no one.
